50:[$09F641]Attilia[$ffffff]: By the Goddess...
51:Malcolm: No, that's impossible:5_00144. Andaro lost. The entire city is destroyed.
52:[$09F641]Attilia[$ffffff]: How can one be so vile...
53:Malcolm: Farewell, friends. May you find solace in death.
54:[$09F641]Attilia[$ffffff]: Will we somehow manage to rebuild the city? I remember it took 30 years to build when it was founded.
55:Malcolm: ...
56:[$09F641]Attilia[$ffffff]: Malcolm? 
57:[$E4DFEC]Eryt[$FFFFFF]: Yes, the whole city is in ruins.
58:Malcolm: Eryt?? Oh yes, I sent him here in mission 6.
59:[$E4DFEC]Eryt[$FFFFFF]: We have to act quickly. Let's implement the plan, and maybe we'll succeed.
60:Malcolm: Give me half an hour, and we'll have the storehouse:5_00133. I'll just gather a team.
61:[$09F641]Attilia[$ffffff]: Maybe we'll succeed? What kind of statement is that? We have to succeed.
62:[$E4DFEC]Eryt[$FFFFFF]: Sorry, but I haven't met you yet. I'm Eryt. 63:[$09F641]Attilia[$ffffff]: And I'm Attilia...
64:[$09F641]Attilia[$ffffff]: Wait a minute... You want to build a storehouse in half an hour? That requires ready-made materials and many builders. Were you lost in your wits?
65:Malcolm: Maybe in my childhood:5_00140, but I don't remember much of that time.
66:Malcolm: Well, there they are. Let's begin, gentlemen.
67:Malcolm: There are no deposits or forests in Andaro. However, I think there's something left over from the war with Valtaria, thirteen years ago, somewhere on the outskirts. If you could, send your men to these areas. Let them see what they can do.
68:Malcolm: And here you go. 
69:[$09F641]Attilia[$ffffff]: Well, I'm impressed. We need to expand further.
70: From now on, Attila's skills are available: |Sniper: her damage, like that of all crossbowmen, is increased |Training: accelerated learning in schools
71:Malcolm: Okay! Now listen. You know what to do, so don't interrupt me! I need to create a weapon to fight "The Guest."
72:[$09F641]Attilia[$ffffff]: Aren't you waiting for Dyron?
73:Malcolm: Who knows if he'll find a way. He went to ask Iris for advice. And who knows if she'll tell him how to defeat him. 
74:[$09F641]Attilia[$ffffff]: You told me that when you fought my brother in Valtaria, he came with Truth's own axe and armor.
75:Malcolm: Only then was he certain such a thing existed. And now he's gone JUST to ask Iris for advice.
76:[$09F641]Attilia[$ffffff]: So what are you planning?
77:Malcolm: Give me some time. I'll work on my project.
78:Malcolm: Attention, test number one.
79:Malcolm: And a failure.
80:Malcolm: Test number two.
81:Malcolm: Also a failure.
82:Malcolm: Now it has to work.
83:Malcolm: And it works. 
84:[$09F641]Attilia[$ffffff]: Impressive. It's like a crossbow, only...
85:Malcolm: A giant version. A ballista. The greatest terror of old.
86:[$09F641]Attilia[$ffffff]: Malcolm, what have you done?! You broke the tractate. We've lived without siege machines for over 400 years, and you want to ruin it?
87:Malcolm: Forgive me, Attilia, but current problems require new solutions. I doubt we'll convince the enemy with diplomacy.
88:[$09F641]Attilia[$ffffff]: Only from now on... I mean... Even if we defeat "The Guest," the other capitals will attack us.
89:Malcolm: They'll have to figure it out somehow, and our "Guest" won't have time to understand what happened. 
90:[$09F641]Attilia[$ffffff]: You're incredibly optimistic.
91:Gather your troops to assault Valtaria. You'll see their number in the panel next to the minimap, which you can expand with the arrow :4_00004:4_00005